WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.825
This video sets the period of a run,
starts the run,

00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:07.980
and reads the daily flow at the basin
outlet and the water balance.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.910
The page is on Set-up.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:16.800
The basin 02070002 North Branch Potomac is
in the list Models.

00:00:17.302 --> 00:00:23.172
The model comes with the years 1997 to
2025 and a warm-up of 3 years.

00:00:23.672 --> 00:00:26.912
In First year, type 1970 and press Enter.

00:00:27.413 --> 00:00:32.323
The page refuses the year, because the
model's weather starts in 1981.

00:00:32.825 --> 00:00:35.865
Now type 2000 in First year and press
Enter.

00:00:36.365 --> 00:00:39.315
In Last year, type 2015 and press Enter.

00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:41.265
In Warm-up, leave 3.

00:00:42.165 --> 00:00:45.555
The run now covers 16 years, the first 3
as warm-up.

00:00:45.755 --> 00:00:48.955
The tables hold 2003 to 2015.

00:00:49.456 --> 00:00:51.376
The first 3 years are the warm-up.

00:00:51.576 --> 00:00:56.400
They are simulated but not written to the
tables, so that the soil water, the snow,

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.957
the groundwater and the plant cover can
move

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.456
away from the values the model starts
with.

00:01:01.956 --> 00:01:05.807
Under Entire basin, Water balance carries
its four ticks:

00:01:05.807 --> 00:01:07.766
day, month, year and average.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:10.291
SWATrust adds the tick under Day,

00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:14.888
because the Results view draws from that
table, and says so under the list.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.700
Leave the other ticks as they are, and
click Continue to Run.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:24.893
The table lists each basin with its years,
its warm-up and the word ready.

00:01:25.093 --> 00:01:29.173
Checks before the run has one line for
each thing that SWATrust checked.

00:01:29.675 --> 00:01:30.855
Click Start the run.

00:01:33.525 --> 00:01:38.135
The line of the basin reads Running and
says what the engine has done so far.

00:01:57.663 --> 00:01:59.283
The state now reads Finished.

00:02:02.223 --> 00:02:03.453
Click See the results.

00:02:08.551 --> 00:02:11.311
The Results view opens on the basin you
just ran.

00:02:11.511 --> 00:02:16.191
The box Basin at the top of the left
column lists the basins that have results.

00:02:16.692 --> 00:02:21.624
In the middle column, the chart under the
basin draws the simulated

00:02:21.624 --> 00:02:27.292
flow at the basin outlet in m³/s from
2003, the first year after the warm-up.

00:02:27.793 --> 00:02:31.753
To look at a part of the period, click
Zoom and draw a box on the chart.

00:02:38.044 --> 00:02:40.124
Zoom out shows the whole period again.

00:02:41.807 --> 00:02:45.507
Under the chart, a small table gives five
figures of the flow.

00:02:45.707 --> 00:02:51.310
The low flow is passed on 95 days in 100
and the high flow on 5 days in 100,

00:02:51.310 --> 00:02:54.037
over the years written to the tables.

00:02:54.537 --> 00:03:00.216
On the left, Water balance, average year
shows the parts of the water balance of the

00:03:00.216 --> 00:03:04.947
land for the average of the years written
to the tables, 2003 to 2015.

00:03:05.147 --> 00:03:08.187
Each part is given in mm over the land
area of

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:11.227
the basin and as a share of the
precipitation.

00:03:11.728 --> 00:03:13.478
The last row, Outlet flow,

00:03:13.478 --> 00:03:17.988
is the mean flow at the basin outlet as a
depth over the same land.

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:22.015
The i beside the heading says that not
every part is listed,

00:03:22.015 --> 00:03:23.719
so the parts need not add up.

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:28.467
Output checks, above it, gives a few of
the same values as shares:

00:03:28.467 --> 00:03:32.908
evapotranspiration and surface runoff as
shares of the precipitation,

00:03:32.908 --> 00:03:35.547
and baseflow as a share of the water that

00:03:35.547 --> 00:03:38.379
the land and the aquifers give the
channels.

00:03:38.881 --> 00:03:42.071
The values of each year are in a file of
the run folder.

00:03:42.271 --> 00:03:45.581
The next chapter, Find the outputs, goes
through that folder.
